From 28e4af5c083024decd6f2709f84e662aec41db88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 07:12:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: lift TQ3_4S kernel set from tq3/master (14 files)

Ports the TQ3_4S (our type 48) CUDA support surgically from the tq3
fork tip: dequant (convert.cu), get_rows, PRMT vec_dot + dedicated
4-warp ncols1 decode kernel (mmvq), MMQ tile loader + Ampere configs +
template instance, Blackwell NVFP4 weight-conversion cache/transient
path (Option E), and the fused Walsh-Hadamard activation rotation in
quantize_row_q8_1_cuda keyed on type_src0. tq3-native.cu/.cuh come
along because mmq.cu/quantize.cu/ggml-cuda.cu include them - the
census 12-file list undercounts by these two.

Tip state carries the 5f60c3929 (MMQ dispatch + rotated Q8_1
activations) and 94e033d7e (out-of-place rotation) fix semantics by
construction. Sibling tq3 types (TQ3_0/TQ3_4SE/TQ3_1S_SHIFT and tq3's
own TQ3_1S, which is NOT our 45) are trimmed out: no enum or wrong
enum on this tree. ggml_cuda_should_use_mmq now takes the tensor so
the TQ3_4S gates can read name/shape.

NOT BUILT HERE: this rig has no CUDA device or toolchain. Compile
readiness only; hardware validation is an OWED row with verbatim
commands in the lane evidence (HARDWARE-VALIDATION.md).

Taken-from: turbo-tan/llama.cpp-tq3@854516439
Origin: lane-160 TQ3_4S hunk port (cherry-pick impossible: trees diverge by whole subsystems); TQ3_4S-only trim + upstream-b10488 adaptation
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED ON THIS RIG (no CUDA silicon); tq3-side references: RTX 3090 tg128 43.1 -> 47.4 t/s (PRMT vec_dot), Ampere decode +35% (3d3888c9f)
Lane: lane-160
